WEBVTT

00:02.440 --> 00:04.560
<b>Bota Bota Yaki</b>

00:02.440 --> 00:04.560
<b>Youkan</b>

00:06.840 --> 00:08.950
What should we do today, Maple?

00:09.510 --> 00:11.110
Good question...

00:19.190 --> 00:20.750
Hello in there!

00:21.250 --> 00:22.570
Frederica?

00:22.570 --> 00:23.960
What brings you here?

00:24.180 --> 00:27.460
Let's have a duel! You 
know, like we always do!

00:27.460 --> 00:29.720
You really never learn, do you?

00:30.300 --> 00:33.630
That confidence of yours 
is gonna be short-lived!

00:34.590 --> 00:37.180
Ooh! You tamed a monster, too?

00:37.180 --> 00:40.390
I sure did. And it's a cute one.

00:40.390 --> 00:42.510
A cute one?

00:42.510 --> 00:44.940
A cute one, huh?

00:48.330 --> 00:57.160
<b>BOFURI: </b>I <b>Don't Want </b>to <b>Get Hurt,
</b>so I'll <b>Max Out My Defense</b>.

02:15.190 --> 02:16.990
<b>BOFURI: </b>I <b>Don't Want </b>to <b>Get Hurt,
</b>so I'll <b>Max Out My Defense</b>.

02:17.630 --> 02:22.340
<b>Maxing Defense </b>and <b>Hunting for Crystals</b>.

02:19.780 --> 02:21.650
Okay, just like always.

02:21.650 --> 02:23.490
Yep. Just like always.

02:24.950 --> 02:26.980
Rooting for you, Sally!

02:26.980 --> 02:28.040
Turtle!

02:34.380 --> 02:35.670
Okay, then...

02:35.670 --> 02:36.710
All right!

02:37.760 --> 02:39.260
[Super Speed]!

02:39.680 --> 02:40.550
Huh?!

02:40.550 --> 02:42.530
Oboro! [Vanish]! [Shadow Clone]!

02:44.190 --> 02:45.140
M-Multi—

02:45.140 --> 02:46.250
[Flash Flood]!

02:46.250 --> 02:47.980
Oboro! [Binding Barrier]!

02:50.730 --> 02:52.690
A stun attack?! I can't move—

02:55.110 --> 02:57.250
Whoa! W-Wait!

02:57.250 --> 02:59.190
[Quintuple Slash]!

03:07.790 --> 03:08.950
Hey!

03:08.950 --> 03:12.360
That's the first time I ever felt 
like you really wanted to <i>kill</i> me!

03:12.360 --> 03:13.940
Must be your imagination.

03:13.940 --> 03:17.840
And I came here to introduce 
you to my partner...

03:17.840 --> 03:20.050
Ooh! What's it like?

03:20.050 --> 03:21.490
Hang on, Maple!

03:21.490 --> 03:23.350
Okay, I'll show you.

03:23.350 --> 03:25.350
Wait... H-Hang on!

03:25.350 --> 03:26.360
[Awaken]!

03:30.540 --> 03:31.440
Peep.

03:32.120 --> 03:34.150
Aww! It's so cute!

03:34.430 --> 03:36.750
This little one's name is Notes.

03:36.750 --> 03:37.730
Peep, peep!

03:37.730 --> 03:39.470
A ch-chick?!

03:39.970 --> 03:44.180
What's wrong? Did you think it 
was gonna be something scary?

03:44.180 --> 03:45.950
F-Frederica!

03:45.950 --> 03:49.450
Whew, thank goodness! If it 
was some kind of ghost...

03:52.750 --> 03:54.890
Wouldn't want to get bitten 
by one of those, huh?

03:54.890 --> 03:59.720
Besides, I wouldn't tame an undead 
monster just to scare Sally.

03:59.720 --> 04:01.230
J-Jeez!

04:01.230 --> 04:03.690
Look at it, Sally! It's so cute!

04:03.690 --> 04:05.680
It's more than just cute...

04:04.550 --> 04:05.680
Rawr!

04:06.180 --> 04:07.270
The wait is over!

04:07.270 --> 04:10.300
It's time to announce the eighth event!

04:10.640 --> 04:14.730
This one will be split up into 
a preliminary and a main event.

04:14.730 --> 04:18.350
The preliminary will be a survival 
match among individual players.

04:18.350 --> 04:22.860
You'll get points based on how long you 
survive and how many monsters you defeat.

04:22.860 --> 04:25.720
Area assignments for the 
main event will be decided

04:25.720 --> 04:27.620
starting with the highest-ranked 
in the preliminary.

04:27.620 --> 04:32.290
Of course, the higher your rank, 
the better the rewards you'll get!

04:32.290 --> 04:33.740
Since you'll be competing individually,

04:33.740 --> 04:36.750
having a tamed monster 
will be to your advantage.

04:36.750 --> 04:39.960
I'll let you know more details later!

04:41.010 --> 04:46.050
We're competing individually with a 
ranking? So it's like the first event.

04:46.050 --> 04:49.350
I guess we'll have another strategy 
meeting once the details come out.

04:49.350 --> 04:53.810
We should all try to rank high 
in the preliminary first.

04:53.810 --> 04:57.650
Hey, come on. Putting the 
event aside for now...

04:57.950 --> 04:59.800
How about one more round?

05:00.860 --> 05:02.690
Yikes. It's from Payne.

05:02.690 --> 05:05.010
Did you have something else to do?

05:05.010 --> 05:08.650
No, he just says not to 
reveal too much to you.

05:08.650 --> 05:10.870
Oh, well. I'm gonna head back for today.

05:10.870 --> 05:12.700
I'll be back to challenge you again.

05:12.700 --> 05:15.660
Sure. I'll gladly beat you to a pulp again.

05:15.660 --> 05:17.590
Bring it on!

05:17.590 --> 05:20.380
I'll show you what Notes here can do!

05:21.020 --> 05:22.840
Bye!

05:24.700 --> 05:28.340
Frederica's chick might be 
good at buffs or debuffs.

05:28.340 --> 05:29.410
You think so?

05:29.410 --> 05:30.950
Just guessing.

05:30.950 --> 05:35.000
It doesn't seem to be an attack specialist 
like May and Yui's bears, y'know?

05:35.000 --> 05:37.900
If anything, it seems closer to Iz's partner.

05:37.900 --> 05:40.790
Oh, yeah, it might be the support type!

05:40.790 --> 05:42.380
And it was cute, too!

05:42.380 --> 05:44.650
Putting its cuteness aside...

05:44.650 --> 05:48.110
If they can accentuate a player's 
strengths or cover for their weaknesses,

05:48.110 --> 05:50.320
having a monster companion 
can really change the game.

05:50.660 --> 05:52.110
That's true.

05:53.310 --> 05:57.050
So where should we go? Doesn't seem like 
the others will be back anytime soon.

05:57.050 --> 05:59.960
Oh, I'd like to explore Level 7, then!

05:59.960 --> 06:03.300
I haven't done anything 
with you in a long time.

06:03.300 --> 06:04.970
Okay. Where should we go?

06:05.550 --> 06:06.630
Let me see...

06:06.630 --> 06:12.600
Lake

06:06.630 --> 06:12.600
Mountains

06:06.630 --> 06:12.600
City of the Great Tree

06:06.630 --> 06:12.600
Floating Island

06:06.630 --> 06:12.600
Ocean

06:06.630 --> 06:12.600
Ruins

06:06.630 --> 06:12.600
Iceberg

06:06.630 --> 06:12.600
Snowy Mountain

06:06.630 --> 06:12.600
Desert

06:06.630 --> 06:12.600
Jungle

06:06.630 --> 06:12.600
Volcano

06:06.900 --> 06:10.140
I've been to the ocean, and 
I saw the forest and volcano.

06:10.140 --> 06:12.600
What other places would look nice?

06:12.600 --> 06:14.850
You're talking like this 
is a pleasure cruise.

06:14.850 --> 06:16.920
Want to just wander around 
and check things out, then?

06:16.920 --> 06:19.780
Yeah! It's been ages since we 
just took time to walk around!

06:19.780 --> 06:21.450
Oh, walking?

06:21.450 --> 06:24.070
I guess I could carry you on my back, but...

06:24.070 --> 06:27.280
Oh, yeah! I've got just the thing!

06:27.280 --> 06:28.650
You do?

06:28.650 --> 06:29.740
Turtle?

06:31.610 --> 06:32.740
It's so fast!

06:32.740 --> 06:35.190
Hold on tight, Maple!

06:35.190 --> 06:37.450
Not that you'd get hurt 
if you fell, but still!

06:38.510 --> 06:39.700
This is awesome!

06:39.700 --> 06:42.600
These are treated like mounts 
rather than tame monsters.

06:42.600 --> 06:45.690
And I found a great horse. 
Pretty fast, isn't it?

06:45.690 --> 06:47.490
That's my Sally!

06:52.640 --> 06:56.500
It doesn't look like there are 
any hostile monsters here.

06:56.500 --> 06:58.670
It won't be the best for leveling up, but...

06:58.670 --> 06:59.350
Yep!

06:59.570 --> 07:02.150
It's perfect for taking 
our time wandering around!

07:33.930 --> 07:36.390
Where the heck did Maple go?

07:36.390 --> 07:38.370
Hey, Maple!

07:38.370 --> 07:39.590
What's up?

07:39.590 --> 07:40.740
Wait, where are you?

07:40.740 --> 07:42.330
Right here!

07:47.550 --> 07:48.760
Oh...

07:49.800 --> 07:51.380
There you are.

07:52.070 --> 07:53.640
What are you doing?

07:54.770 --> 07:57.860
These guys just kept bouncing 
me up into the air,

07:57.860 --> 07:59.470
and now they're giving me a ride!

07:59.470 --> 08:02.080
I think they're just playing with you.

08:02.080 --> 08:04.970
Aw, don't worry about it! C'mon in here!

08:07.670 --> 08:11.410
It's nice taking it easy 
every now and then, isn't it?

08:15.970 --> 08:17.990
Isn't that what you always do anyway?

08:17.990 --> 08:21.520
Huh? I don't think I do...

08:22.390 --> 08:23.220
What the?!

08:23.220 --> 08:24.570
Maple, get inside!

08:28.860 --> 08:30.190
I'm getting dizzy!

08:38.490 --> 08:40.760
The world's spinning...

08:40.760 --> 08:42.610
Where are we, anyway?

08:45.340 --> 08:46.530
[Wool Hunting]!

08:50.380 --> 08:52.540
Water... Water...

09:04.740 --> 09:05.690
<i>Gulp...</i>

09:10.250 --> 09:12.260
Wh-Why?!

09:12.260 --> 09:13.650
Maple?!

09:14.130 --> 09:15.240
[Web User]!

09:19.540 --> 09:20.930
You okay?

09:20.930 --> 09:22.740
That startled me...

09:22.740 --> 09:25.140
They must've thought you were gonna eat them.

09:25.140 --> 09:27.640
Aw, I wouldn't eat them!

09:27.640 --> 09:29.290
I wonder about that...

09:32.800 --> 09:34.920
Maple, did you drop something?

09:34.920 --> 09:38.730
No, I don't think I dropped anything...

09:38.730 --> 09:39.640
Look.

09:40.210 --> 09:41.560
Something's there!

09:42.600 --> 09:44.050
I wonder what it is.

09:44.770 --> 09:45.560
Turtle!

09:45.560 --> 09:47.110
Syrup?

09:49.520 --> 09:50.950
Turtle.

09:53.310 --> 09:54.460
A crystal?

09:54.460 --> 09:55.720
Let's see...

09:55.720 --> 10:01.300
"White Key. One of three keys that can 
be used to unlock a certain door."

10:01.300 --> 10:02.710
This is a key?

10:02.710 --> 10:06.870
If there are three, that means there 
are two others like it somewhere.

10:06.870 --> 10:09.960
It's not gonna be easy to look 
for something this small.

10:09.960 --> 10:11.720
Yeah, we need some kind of hint.

10:11.720 --> 10:15.200
This quest started before we 
even knew what was going on,

10:15.200 --> 10:18.200
but there must be some 
condition for triggering it.

10:18.200 --> 10:20.890
Condition for triggering it...

10:21.540 --> 10:23.600
Traveling monsters...

10:25.660 --> 10:26.170
Huh?

10:26.170 --> 10:29.920
We were carried here by those sheep, right?

10:29.920 --> 10:31.670
So I just thought, maybe...

10:31.670 --> 10:35.380
Why don't we check for other traveling 
monsters while we look around?

10:35.380 --> 10:36.980
Yeah, I'm in!

10:36.980 --> 10:41.180
And if we find another one, that'll 
mean your guess was right!

10:41.180 --> 10:44.240
Yeah, I dunno if it'll be that simple...

10:44.590 --> 10:47.330
But I figure it beats just searching blindly.

10:49.660 --> 10:52.470
Sally! You got this!

11:02.590 --> 11:03.890
<i>Is that...</i>

11:11.400 --> 11:12.630
<i>I knew it!</i>

11:27.200 --> 11:28.430
<i>What's that?</i>

11:43.060 --> 11:45.010
A map of Level 7?

11:45.010 --> 11:48.990
It's obviously something meant 
to be used in some event.

11:48.990 --> 11:49.790
Yeah!

11:49.790 --> 11:52.520
Uh, there are all kinds 
of marks on it, though...

11:52.520 --> 11:56.730
Look. There's a mark on the area 
where we found that spring.

11:56.730 --> 12:01.570
I bet one of these is where we want 
to go, and the rest have clues.

12:03.450 --> 12:05.950
An event map, huh?

12:08.620 --> 12:10.890
Does it look familiar at all?

12:10.890 --> 12:15.010
Well... I saw some relevant 
info at the library.

12:15.010 --> 12:16.400
Really?

12:16.400 --> 12:16.940
Yeah.

12:16.940 --> 12:17.840
Really? <i>There</i>?!

12:17.840 --> 12:20.150
In the past, there were prosperous cities,

12:20.150 --> 12:24.580
and there, people could bond with 
monsters even more than we do now.

12:24.580 --> 12:25.890
No! Don't!

12:25.890 --> 12:30.520
On the map, those cities would be here and...

12:31.980 --> 12:34.450
Aw, I lose.

12:34.450 --> 12:36.060
I give up.

12:36.060 --> 12:38.330
Oh! The location of that spring is here, too!

12:38.330 --> 12:39.830
This is great info!

12:39.830 --> 12:42.620
I'm impressed you knew this. 
Did you just happen to find it?

12:42.620 --> 12:44.690
No, I've read them all.

12:44.690 --> 12:45.550
Huh?!

12:45.550 --> 12:47.100
The books in the library?!

12:47.100 --> 12:48.410
<i>All</i> of them?!

12:48.410 --> 12:49.910
They're really interesting,

12:49.910 --> 12:53.890
and some of them contain hints to 
help with events, like this one.

12:53.890 --> 12:57.630
You should read them sometime. 
It'll take a while, though.

12:58.470 --> 13:00.840
You never cease to amaze me.

13:00.840 --> 13:03.660
I don't think we'll ever 
win a game against Kanade.

13:03.660 --> 13:04.340
Yeah.

13:04.340 --> 13:06.400
Well, shall we get going?

13:06.400 --> 13:07.300
Yeah!

13:07.300 --> 13:10.640
I'm looking forward to good news, you two.

13:10.640 --> 13:14.770
May and Yui, keep doing 
your best to beat Kanade!

13:14.770 --> 13:17.500
Okay, we'll try...

13:34.110 --> 13:36.820
Looks like the same system as 
the boss in the second event.

13:36.820 --> 13:38.780
It might have similar attacks, too.

13:38.780 --> 13:42.170
Then we'll have to show it how 
much stronger we've gotten!

13:45.130 --> 13:47.530
Syrup! [Mother Nature]! [Thorn Shackles]!

13:47.530 --> 13:49.590
And then, [Sleep Petals]!

13:54.150 --> 13:55.100
[Path of Water]!

13:57.290 --> 13:58.940
[Quintuple Slash]!

13:58.940 --> 14:00.150
[Spirit Cannon]!

14:00.150 --> 14:02.110
Tur...

14:02.110 --> 14:04.180
...tle!

14:06.040 --> 14:09.110
Okay! [Deploy Armaments]!

14:10.740 --> 14:12.390
[Invitation to the Ocean Floor]!

14:12.950 --> 14:13.990
[Predator]!

14:20.130 --> 14:21.140
[Devour]!

14:21.140 --> 14:22.250
[Seeping Chaos]!

14:22.250 --> 14:23.590
[Commence Attack]!

14:32.810 --> 14:34.630
Yikes...

14:36.810 --> 14:38.280
And to finish it...

14:38.620 --> 14:39.730
[Hydra]!

14:46.530 --> 14:48.490
All right! We won!

14:49.620 --> 14:52.580
I feel sorry for anyone who 
has to take her on in PvP.

14:52.580 --> 14:52.990
Wait!

14:53.310 --> 14:54.870
Crystal! Crystal!

14:55.200 --> 14:58.330
Green Key

14:55.200 --> 14:58.330
One of three keys that can be used to unlock a certain door.

14:56.410 --> 14:58.330
Yep! The Green Key.

14:58.330 --> 15:01.230
"One of three keys that can be 
used to unlock a certain door."

15:01.230 --> 15:03.490
We got the second key, Sally!

15:03.490 --> 15:07.350
So, Kanade told us about 
one other location...

15:07.350 --> 15:10.860
I can't use [Devour] anymore, 
but if you're still good...

15:10.860 --> 15:13.760
Yeah, there's plenty of time, 
so we might as well go there.

15:13.760 --> 15:14.680
Yeah!

15:18.990 --> 15:20.950
Wow, this place feels weird!

15:20.950 --> 15:24.050
And the wind is intense. 
It might blow us away.

15:24.050 --> 15:26.140
The moment you said that, 
something came flying at <i>us</i>!

15:26.140 --> 15:26.780
Huh?!

15:29.010 --> 15:30.200
M-Maple?!

15:31.730 --> 15:33.990
You flew pretty far. You okay?

15:33.990 --> 15:35.740
That caught me by surprise...

15:35.740 --> 15:39.870
But thank goodness it wasn't 
piercing or terrain damage.

15:40.210 --> 15:41.940
Glad to see you're okay.

15:58.680 --> 16:01.490
Looks strong. We'd better go in swinging!

16:01.490 --> 16:02.890
Yep! Leave it to me!

16:06.420 --> 16:07.350
Wait!

16:07.350 --> 16:10.070
I wasn't ready yet!

16:12.010 --> 16:14.770
I don't think I can save you from that one...

16:14.770 --> 16:16.930
Whoa! I gotta focus, too!

16:20.040 --> 16:21.450
[Super Speed]!

16:22.010 --> 16:24.500
Oboro! [Fairy Fire]! [Fire Child]!

16:28.290 --> 16:29.310
Yes!

16:46.180 --> 16:48.030
She's really going crazy...

16:48.610 --> 16:51.230
Well, I just gotta do what I can do, right?

16:52.840 --> 16:56.020
[Power Attack]!

17:13.670 --> 17:15.420
Oboro! [Spirited Away]!

17:34.030 --> 17:37.770
Great job! You kinda looked like a ninja!

17:38.620 --> 17:40.430
And here's what we were after.

17:40.430 --> 17:42.830
The third key! Yay!

17:42.830 --> 17:45.210
That just leaves the ruins 
Kanade told us about.

17:45.210 --> 17:47.190
Let's go!

18:06.140 --> 18:07.970
What is this place?

18:07.970 --> 18:10.120
Yeah, it's kinda weird...

18:10.120 --> 18:11.110
Syrup?

18:11.110 --> 18:12.850
Oboro, where are you going?

18:12.850 --> 18:14.350
What's wrong with them?

18:14.350 --> 18:16.440
Let's follow Oboro and see.

18:23.700 --> 18:25.390
Hey, look, Maple!

18:25.390 --> 18:27.910
So many critters I've never seen before!

18:58.900 --> 19:01.080
This place looks kind of important.

19:01.080 --> 19:04.230
Yeah, and I don't think 
this is ordinary water.

19:06.930 --> 19:09.320
Nothing weird's gonna happen, is it?

19:09.320 --> 19:10.750
N-Nah...

19:14.700 --> 19:15.720
Huh?!

19:16.870 --> 19:19.090
A-Are you okay, Syrup?!

19:21.070 --> 19:23.010
O-Oboro?

19:24.970 --> 19:25.970
Turtle!

19:28.770 --> 19:29.730
Huh?

19:32.550 --> 19:34.700
They evolved?!

19:36.030 --> 19:37.480
They're so cute!

19:37.780 --> 19:39.820
Evolution? So they evolved!

19:40.050 --> 19:41.740
Yes, very interesting!

19:41.740 --> 19:44.550
It seems like they get new 
skills when they evolve.

19:44.550 --> 19:47.340
Syrup looks a little more stylish now!

19:47.340 --> 19:49.410
And a little bigger too, maybe?

19:49.410 --> 19:50.500
Turtle!

19:51.160 --> 19:53.290
You've really grown up.

19:53.290 --> 19:55.470
We've fought a lot of battles together, huh?

19:55.470 --> 19:57.720
But it seems like they can still go further.

19:57.720 --> 19:59.100
Really?

19:59.100 --> 20:02.730
Yeah. There's nothing in the explanation 
saying that they only evolve once.

20:02.730 --> 20:05.790
But you know, if it makes 
them this much stronger,

20:05.790 --> 20:07.390
let's make all our companions evolve!

20:07.700 --> 20:10.080
I bet if we complete the event...

20:10.080 --> 20:13.300
Well, of course, it'd be 
great if we could, but...

20:13.300 --> 20:17.400
I went to the place with the floating 
rocks, too, but I didn't see any giant.

20:17.400 --> 20:19.950
And I went to the top of the Great Tree,

20:19.950 --> 20:22.490
but I didn't get any events or battles.

20:22.490 --> 20:24.320
What does that mean?

20:24.320 --> 20:29.010
Um... Maybe its level and how friendly 
it is with you are involved?

20:29.010 --> 20:33.220
Right, Maple and Sally have been with 
Syrup and Oboro for a long time.

20:33.220 --> 20:37.320
The book said something about bringing 
out their strengths more, too.

20:37.320 --> 20:40.050
Maybe you have to get their basic 
abilities to a certain point first.

20:40.500 --> 20:44.180
So it really is because 
we've been together for so long?

20:49.430 --> 20:51.570
Too many new features!

20:51.570 --> 20:53.790
Ugh, all these little bugs everywhere!

20:53.790 --> 20:56.940
If you've got time to gripe, 
use it to work instead!

20:56.940 --> 20:59.730
Hey! How many rare monsters 
have been consumed?

20:59.730 --> 21:01.240
Less than 20%.

21:01.240 --> 21:06.200
It's a big area, so there are many strong 
monsters, even if they aren't rare.

21:06.200 --> 21:08.530
We all worked hard to pull this together.

21:08.530 --> 21:09.900
How are the major guilds doing?

21:09.900 --> 21:11.800
This one is swimming in rare monsters.

21:11.800 --> 21:12.660
Dang, they're strong!

21:12.660 --> 21:15.330
They're seriously grabbing 
all the good stuff.

21:15.330 --> 21:18.210
By the way, how will you 
be handling the next event?

21:18.210 --> 21:20.510
If the players are gonna become monsters,

